      "title": "Finding the Rank or Nullity of a Matrix Given a Description of the Column or Null Space"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c003d45c-de23-5996-8edf-94f99545d30c",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Let $A$ be a $7\\times 8$ matrix. If $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},{b}_{4},{b}_{5},{b}_{6},{b}_{7}\\}$ is a basis of $\\text{Col}(A)$, find $\\text{dim(Null}(A)).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=8,$ and since $B$ is formed by $7$ vectors, $\\text{rank}(A)=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 7+\\text{nullity}(A) & =8 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =8-7 \\\\ \\text{dim(Null}(A)) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "efbc1209-c9f5-5b87-8c33-f916c3db7a74",
